# Committed generated goldens must stay LF regardless of a contributor's core.autocrlf, or the
# byte-diff freshness gates (audit-gates.sh 146-150) drift forever on a Windows/CRLF checkout
# (FORGE /wireframe v1.1 tiebreak T11 / red-team R3): git would normalize a committed LF golden to
# CRLF in the working tree while the emitter still produces LF, so the byte-diff can never match.
*.mmd text eol=lf
*.svg text eol=lf
*.txt text eol=lf

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The task ledger is an APPEND-ONLY event log. Concurrent worktrees append to the
# same file, so a default 3-way merge conflicts on every parallel session.
#
# ⛔ MEASURED 2026-08-19, WITH A CONTROL, before this line was written:
#   two divergent branches each appending -> union merge = 5 lines, ZERO loss,
#   zero conflict markers; the SAME scenario WITHOUT this attribute CONFLICTS
#   (exit 1). The control fires, so the union driver is the mechanism and the
#   clean result is real rather than incidental.
#
# ⛔ SCOPED TO THE LEDGER PATH, never a blanket `*.jsonl`. A blanket rule would
#   also union-merge tests/fixtures/ledger/*.jsonl, whose EXACT BYTES are the
#   assertion — silently corrupting the fixtures that prove the ledger works.
#   Verified: check-attr reports `union` for the ledger path and `unspecified`
#   for the fixture path.
#
# ⛔ union does NOT make dedupe unnecessary. It dedupes only BYTE-IDENTICAL lines
#   (measured); two records sharing an event_id but differing in any byte both
#   survive, so ledger.py still dedupes by event_id at projection. git's own docs
#   warn union leaves lines "in random order" — hence the total-order sort in the
#   projection, never reliance on file order.
.ravenclaude/ledger/*.jsonl merge=union
